ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":140,"prev":142,"next":145,"titles":148,"firmware":66},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":30,"procedures":72,"parameters":100,"related":113,"body":120,"sources":121,"official_url":34,"controls":133},"instrument.engine-midi","Midi engine (called external in the guide)",[5,6,7,8,9],"midi engine","external","external engine","external midi engine","sequence an external synth","instrument",50,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/engine-midi.md",{"modes":14,"screens":15},[10],[16,17,18],"M1","M2","M3","The midi engine makes an instrument track sequence outside gear — `M1` sets channel, bank and program, `M2` and `M3` hold eight CCs. TE's guide still calls it external, its name before OS 1.0.15.","outdated-in-guide",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":27,"verified_on":29},"1.0.9",[24,25,26,27,28],"1.0.15","1.0.45","1.0.50","1.1.15","1.1.32",null,[31,36,39,43,46,50,54,58,62,68],{"id":32,"text":33,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"what","The midi engine makes no sound; the track's notes and settings go out as MIDI to an external instrument.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/synth-engines#external","official",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"channel","A midi-engine track sends on the channel chosen with `E1` on its `M1` page; the guide does not tie it to the project's MIDI channels.",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":42,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"renamed","OS 1.0.15 renamed the engine from external to midi; the guide (v1.1.15) and its MIDI how-to still use the old name.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.15",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"cc-slots","`M2` and `M3` hold eight CC slots: turn an encoder to set a value, or hold `shift` and turn it to switch the slot on and choose its CC number.",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":49,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"several-devices","Several instrument tracks can run the midi engine at once, one per device or channel, where the external MIDI track in auxiliary mode offers only one.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#how-to-control-a-synth-with-midi",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":53,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"presets-keep-ccs","Since OS 1.0.45, presets saved from a midi-engine track keep their CC settings.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.45",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":57,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"switch-back","Since OS 1.0.50, switching a track to the midi engine and back keeps its synth settings.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.50",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":61,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"program-locks","Program changes can be parameter-locked per step; OS 1.1.15 fixed such locks not working.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.15",{"id":63,"text":64,"source":65,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":66,"confidence":67},"browser-1133","On OS 1.1.33 the preset browser that `shift + M1` brings up listed no midi engine, so how that firmware puts an instrument track on midi is still open; the external MIDI track (auxiliary `T3`) always works, and this app's replica lists midi last in the browser.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#26-preset-browser-shift--m1","1.1.33","verified",{"id":69,"text":70,"source":71,"firmware_min":28,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"arp-fix","OS 1.1.32 fixed the arpeggiator disturbing a midi-engine parameter.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.32",[73],{"id":74,"goal":75,"preconditions":76,"steps":79,"result":99,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"setup","Sequence an external synth from an instrument track",[77,78],"instrument mode","the synth is connected over USB or to t